<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nyantio</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The nyantio were the warrior aristocracy of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaabu-empire">Kaabu Empire</a> in the Senegambian region. Kaabu grew from a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a> into an autonomous empire under their leadership as Mali weakened in the fifteenth century. Provincial rulers were drawn from the nyantio, but divisions among them, together with the rise of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fula</a> Islamic states, contributed to Kaabu's decline.</p></div>
